{"timestamp": "2026-02-04 19:55:10.994386", "event": "llm_start", "messages": "content='Based on the diagnosis report: ### Troubleshooting Diagnosis Report\\n\\n#### Network Health Overview:\\nThe network is a 4-tier data center Clos topology using EBGP for routing. It includes DNS servers, web servers, and external client hosts. The reachability test results indicate that there are issues with connectivity between hosts.\\n\\n#### Observations:\\n1. **Reachability Test Results**:\\n   - **Client to DNS Server (`client_0` to `dns_pod0`)**:\\n     - Status: Unknown\\n     - No data on transmitted packets, received packets, or round-trip time.\\n   - **DNS Server to Client (`dns_pod0` to `client_0`)**:\\n     - Status: Unknown\\n     - No data on transmitted packets, received packets, or round-trip time.\\n   - **Web Server to Client (`webserver0_pod0` to `client_0`)**:\\n     - Status: Unknown\\n     - No data on transmitted packets, received packets, or round-trip time.\\n   - **Web Server to DNS Server (`webserver0_pod0` to `dns_pod0`)**:\\n     - Status: Unknown\\n     - No data on transmitted packets, received packets, or round-trip time.\\n\\n2. **Connectivity Issues**:\\n   - All reachability tests between hosts have returned a status of \"unknown,\" indicating potential anomalies in the network. This could be due to routing issues, service failures, or misconfigurations.\\n\\n#### Next Steps:\\nTo further diagnose the root cause of the connectivity issues, I will investigate:\\n- The network configuration of the hosts and routers.\\n- The status of BGP sessions and routing tables on the routers.\\n- The operational status of services (DNS and HTTP servers).\\n- Any potential issues with the physical or virtual interfaces.\\n\\nWould you like me to proceed with specific checks or gather more detailed information?, please provide the submission. Do not submit if no report available.' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={} id='adff3876-ebbf-4724-b077-c819b33e1